WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.300
EvoWorld: Imagine. Act. Evolve.
Real robot footage, 5× speed.

00:05.300 --> 00:11.200
Monolithic robot policies struggle to keep learning, and data stays fragmented across scenes and tasks.
EvoWorld shares the dynamics and specializes the skills.

00:11.200 --> 00:21.400
One loop, four moves: ground the task in a real scene, route it to an expert, imagine the outcome in the world model, and evolve from a VLM diagnosis.

00:21.400 --> 00:23.500
Imagine first: world-model rollouts score candidate experts before anything moves.

00:23.500 --> 00:29.550
World-model rollout, 2× speed. Task: put the yellow block in the blue cup.

00:29.550 --> 00:35.550
World-model rollout, 2× speed. Task: put the cup upright.

00:35.550 --> 00:41.600
World-model rollout, 2× speed. Task: use the white towel to wipe the table.

00:41.600 --> 00:53.600
Then act: a real Franka arm manipulates a towel. Complete 1:55 recording shown at 10× speed.

00:53.600 --> 01:00.800
Mean policy success rises from 25.9% to 44.8% across four VLA backbones (paper, Table 1).
Real-robot success rises from 29% to 70% (5 tasks × 20 trials, rebuttal study).

01:00.800 --> 01:06.000
EvoWorld · ECCV 2026 · doczbs.github.io/EvoWorld
